{title: By His Wounds}
{subtitle: Isaiah 53:3–6}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 65}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Am/C] | [Bb] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He grew up like a tender [Am/C]shoot
[Bb]A root in thirsty [F]ground
[Dm]No beauty there to hold our [Am/C]eyes
No glory to be [Bb]found [C]
[Gm]He was despised and reject[Dm]ed by men
[Bb]A man of sorrows, ac[A]quainted with grief
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But he was [Dm]pierced for our transgressions
[Am/C]Crushed for our iniquities
[Bb]The punishment that brought us peace [Gm]was laid upon him
[Bb]And by his [C]wounds we are [Dm]healed [Am/C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]We hid our faces when he [Am/C]passed
[Bb]We thought that God had struck him [F]down [Am7/E]
[Dm]We never knew the weight he [Am/C]bore
Was ours and not his [Bb]own
[Gm]Yet it was our griefs he [Dm]bore
Our sorrows he car[Bb][A]ried
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But he was [Dm]pierced for our transgressions
[Am/C]Crushed for our iniquities
[Bb]The punishment that brought us peace [Gm]was laid upon him
[Bb]And by his [C]wounds we are [Dm]healed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]All of us have strayed like [Dm]sheep
[Bb]Each one has turned to his own [Dm]way
And the [Bb]LORD has laid on him
The in[Dm]iquity of us all
Like [Gm7]a lamb led to the slaughter
[A]He did not open his [Bb]mouth [Dm]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But he was pierced for our transgressions
[Am/C]Crushed for our iniquities
[Bb]The punishment that brought us peace [Gm]was laid upon him
[Bb]And by his [C]wounds we are [Dm]healed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]By his [C]wounds we are [Dm]healed
{end_of_verse}

